# Push to main by default

When a task is finished and there are commits to publish (or uncommitted work that belongs in the completed task):

1. Commit with a concise message (HEREDOC), excluding secrets, scratch assets, and `supabase/.temp/*`.
2. Push to `origin/main` with a normal `git push` (never `--force` on main).
3. Do this at the end of the task without waiting for an explicit “push” ask.

Still ask first only for destructive git operations, force-push, amending pushed commits, or commits that would include secrets.
